            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of an intramuscular cavernous and capillary hemangioma of the thigh revealed by pains evolving for 2 years and by an amyotrophy. After 21 months of investigation, the surgical excision and the histological examination only established the dia Thigh MRI. T1-weighted axial and sagittal sections with gadolinium infusion.</AbstractText>
